commit e3329c837ec4521bcd521865b6d5bd6693659739
Author: 仓鼠王 <yjianbin419@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 23 02:51:18 2026 +0800

    fix(review): identify the deployed bundle by content, and refuse a port another chain owns (ORD-0226 follow-up ②)
    
    The arm driver walked onto :4781/:4782 -- the preview chain's ports -- and a stack that never
    started exits non-zero just like a kill does, so one arm's verdict was unevidenced. The driver now
    refuses a busy port span up front and reports INVALID_STACK instead of a verdict, and the bundle
    probe hashes the bytes it reads so a generation coordinate is content, not a filename.

